+qsearch fix, 9 Nov 2026 (research/audits/reviews/2026-11-09-lrat-checker-fix/): the upstream copy
+accepted an empty clause without a conflict (any CNF "verified" with the proof `<m+1> 0 0`, or with
+`<m+1> 0 1 -1 0` after line 161 is restored). Changes, marked FIX below: (1) line 161 restored, so
+a lemma without RAT hints must be RUP; (2) the empty clause must be RUP (it has no pivot, so RAT
+hints cannot justify it); (3) unknown clause indices read as DELETED instead of out-of-bounds;
+(4) lemma indices must increase strictly, and the index table grows until the index fits;
+(5) CNF literals beyond the header's variable count are rejected.
